00:36:00,000 --> 00:36:06,000
Black Christmas is a 1974 Canadian slasher film produced and
directed by Bob Clark, and written by Roy Moore.

13
00:39:00,000 --> 00:39:06,000
It stars Olivia Hussey, Keir Dullea, Margot Kidder, and John Saxon.

14
00:42:00,000 --> 00:42:06,000
The story follows a group of sorority sisters who receive threatening phone calls and are
eventually stalked and murdered by a killer during the Christmas season.

15
00:45:00,000 --> 00:45:06,000
Inspired by the urban legend "the babysitter and the man upstairs" and a series of murders that took place in the
Westmount neighbourhood of Montreal, Quebec, Moore wrote the screenplay under the title Stop Me.

16
00:48:00,000 --> 00:48:06,000
The filmmakers made numerous alterations to the script, primarily the
shifting to a university setting with young adult characters.

17
00:51:00,000 --> 00:51:06,000
It was shot in Toronto in 1974 on an estimated budget of $686,000.

18
00:54:00,000 --> 00:54:06,000
The film was released in Canada on October 11, 1974
by Ambassador Film Distributors.

19
00:57:00,000 --> 00:57:06,000
Warner Bros.

20
01:00:00,000 --> 01:00:06,000
released the film in the United States in May 1975 under the alternate title Silent Night, Evil Night, though this
title was retracted and the film was reissued under its original title beginning August 6, 1975.

21
01:03:00,000 --> 01:03:06,000
The film went on to gross $4,053,000 worldwide.

22
01:06:00,000 --> 01:06:06,000
Upon its release, Black Christmas received mixed reviews, but it has since received critical
re-appraisal, with film historians noting it for being one of the earliest slasher films.

23
01:09:00,000 --> 01:09:06,000
It is also praised for its influence on John Carpenter's Halloween (1978).

24
01:12:00,000 --> 01:12:06,000
Aside from it earning a cult following since its release, a
novelization written by Lee Hays was published in 1976.

25
01:15:00,000 --> 01:15:06,000
It is the first film in the Black Christmas series, being
followed by two remakes in 2006 and  2019.

26
01:18:00,000 --> 01:18:06,000
The film explores themes of mistaken identity,
co-workers relationship, toy factory, christmas.

27
01:21:00,000 --> 01:21:06,000
The tone is emotional.
